# Configuration reference (FLOW-160): names and placeholders only.
# Never copy production credentials into this file or Flowbase GitHub Actions.
# Local browser values belong in ignored .env.local; Worker secrets in .dev.vars.
# Cloudflare build variables and Worker runtime secrets are separate settings.

# Worker flowbase -> Settings -> Builds -> Variables and Secrets:
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN: Text in Production and, optionally, Preview. Both may use the
# same Sentry project DSN; use a test project's DSN for separate preview reporting.
# All VITE_* values are public and are included in the browser build.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# DATABASE_URL: Secret in Production builds ONLY, using the real flowbase-prod
# Postgres URI from Supabase -> Connect (session pooler if IPv6 is unavailable).
# Replace the password placeholder and URL-encode special password characters.
# Preview builds do not run migrations, so do not set a Preview DATABASE_URL.
# The value below is ONLY the disposable CI database, never a Cloudflare value.
# drizzle-kit migrate also reads DATABASE_URL; set a dev URI in your own shell
# for manual dev migrations. Never replace this example with a real database URI.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://flowbase:flowbase@localhost:5432/flowbase_ci

# Worker flowbase -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets (runtime):
# SENTRY_DSN: Secret, the Sentry project DSN for Worker error reporting. It may
# match VITE_SENTRY_DSN, but must be configured separately from the build value.
SENTRY_DSN=
# APP_VERSION: optional Text release override; omit to use package.json version.
APP_VERSION=

# File storage (FLOW-42): two runtime Secrets from the same R2 S3 credential,
# with Object Read & Write access to flowbase-files. Production storage only.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID, R2_BUCKET and FILES are configured in wrangler.jsonc.
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Ingestion: runtime Secrets, added when each integration is configured.
# INGEST_TOKEN_LEADS: generated token shared with the private ops collector
# (FLOW-114; collector/README.md). Never put collector credentials in this repo.
# INGEST_TOKEN_THUMBTACK: generated token configured on the Thumbtack webhook
# (FLOW-115). SHOPIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET: Shopify webhook signing secret (FLOW-115).
# Comma-separate old,new while rotating, then remove the old value.
# INGEST_TOKEN_LEADS=
# INGEST_TOKEN_THUMBTACK=
# SHOPIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Preview currently uploads versions of the SAME flowbase Worker, with the dev
# database and no file-storage bindings/vars. Runtime secrets are not isolated
# by the Production/Preview build tabs; do not assume previews are secret-free.
# FLOW-176 tracks preview isolation. Production DATABASE_URL stays build-only.

# Hyperdrive binding HYPERDRIVE is declared per environment in wrangler.jsonc.
# No Supabase URL or API keys are consumed by the current Worker (FLOW-36 adds
# sign-in); Google OAuth client credentials belong in Supabase's Google provider.
# Local-only: `wrangler dev --env dev` (no --remote) needs this connection string
# in your shell or ignored .dev.vars, never in either Cloudflare settings screen:
# CLOUDFLARE_HYPERDRIVE_LOCAL_CONNECTION_STRING_HYPERDRIVE=

# Private ops-repo Actions secrets are documented in collector/README.md and
# docs/restore.md, not configured on the Worker. The collector template expects
# FLOWBASE_READ_TOKEN for the read-only PAT (FLOW-160 called it FLOWBASE_REPO_TOKEN).
